gatm(){return"I forgot my sign-in email: what can I do?"},
gar9(){return"On the sign-in screen, choose Forgot your email? and enter the recovery email you previously added and verified in settings. Choose Send reminder: if the address is linked to an account, that inbox will receive a message with your sign-in email. To protect your privacy, the sign-in address is not displayed on the page."},
gatW(){return"How do I set up a recovery email?"},
gasf(){return"While you still have access to your account, open Settings from the calendar menu and choose Recovery email. The status appears at the top. Enter an address you can access, different from your primary email, and your current password. The eye icon shows or hides your password. Choose Send verification email. Additional guidance is under How it works."},
gasg(){return"Open the link you receive and press Confirm recovery email: opening the link alone is not enough. You can confirm on another device. The link lasts 30 minutes. Return to settings and choose Check verification to check activation. Confirmation does not change your primary email or sign you in."},
gatn(){return"I lost access to my primary inbox: can I recover my account?"},
gara(){return"Yes, if you had already verified a recovery email and enabled full recovery before losing access. On the sign-in screen, choose Forgot your email?, then the option to recover your account with a new email and password. Enter your recovery email and request the link."},
garb(){return"Open the link in your recovery inbox and enter a new address you can access. A second link will be sent there: open it and choose a new password to complete the process. Your credentials change only when recovery is completed. Then sign in with your new email and password: your projects and data remain in the same account, without registering again."},
gatV(){return"What does Email reminders only mean?"},
gase(){return"That contact can remind you of your sign-in address, but cannot let you choose a new email and password. To enable full recovery, open Recovery email in settings, choose Enable full recovery, enter the same address and your current password, and verify the inbox again. Check that the status changes to Full recovery enabled."},
gatT(){return"Can I change or remove my recovery email?"},
gasb(){return"Yes, from Settings > Recovery email. Choose Edit address, enter the new address and your current password, then confirm the link you receive. During replacement, the pending address and previous contact are shown; the previous contact stays valid until confirmation. Cancel in the form only closes editing without sending a request. To remove pending verification when no verified contact exists, use Cancel request. Remove recovery email removes both the verified contact and any pending request, after confirming your current password. Your sign-in email stays the same."},
gatU(){return"The recovery email has not arrived or the link does not work: what should I do?"},
gasc(){return"Check your spam folder and the address you entered. Reminders are sent only to a previously verified contact; account recovery links also require full recovery to have been enabled already. The request received message does not confirm that the address is linked to an account. You can request up to 3 reminders and up to 3 recovery links per address every 24 hours; if you reach a request limit, wait and try again later."},
gasd(){return"For contact verification, return to settings and choose Send again, confirming with your current password: the new link replaces the previous one. If an account recovery link has expired or is invalid, restart from the sign-in screen. If you had not configured a suitable contact, check a device where you are still signed in or use the support contact shown on the recovery page."},
gasu(){return"Password reset requires access to your account inbox. If you cannot remember the address, choose Forgot your email?; if you can no longer open that inbox, see Email and account recovery to use a recovery contact you previously enabled."},
