gatz(){return"Where can I find received announcements?"},
garw(){return"Tap the bell in the calendar to open Notifications. The number shows how many announcements you have not read yet. You can also reopen announcements you have already read."},
garx(){return"The inbox keeps announcements sent by the app administrators, even when push notifications are turned off. It is not a history of all automatic notifications about events, invitations or reminders."},
gatA(){return"Why do messages appear when I open the app?"},
gary(){return"When the app starts, after signing in if needed, unread announcements appear one at a time, oldest first. The sequence does not restart when you return from another app or tab. The counter, for example \u201c1 of 3\u201d, shows your place in the sequence."},
garz(){return"If you launch the app from an announcement push, that announcement appears first, without repeating in the sequence. If the app is already running, tapping a push opens only that notification. Launching the app from an event or reminder push also opens only that notification. Read later stops the popups: the current and remaining announcements stay unread in the bell inbox. Opening an event notification refreshes the project calendar."},
gatB(){return"When is an announcement marked as read?"},
garA(){return"An announcement is marked as read when you press OK in its popup. Read later leaves it unread. If it is already read, the popup only shows Close. Read status is shared across devices using the same account."},
garB(){return"If saving fails, the popup stays open with an error message: press OK again to retry. In the list, Mark all as read confirms all announcements received up to the time the list was loaded."},
gatC(){return"How do I refresh the notifications list?"},
garC(){return"Press the refresh icon at the top right to reload the list. Pulling down does not refresh it. All and Unread filter announcements that have already loaded; use Load more to see earlier announcements when available."},
garD(){return"After OK, the row and count update immediately without reloading the list. Under Unread, the announcement disappears, but you can find it under All. Read later only closes the popup."},
